# Which built-in may be a closure of which function. None is a closure of a function of the application. A native one is a closure of no function. One that is written in JavaScript is a closure of the function the program registers for it and of no other. Where the table does not say what the function object is, as of `eval`, it is a closure of no function that a type names: it gets into such a type as a value, among the built-ins of the type. No type says that a built-in is a closure, so the subset relation answers no, and the intersection names the object as its second operand does
